    "question": "Apple can run at a rate of 3 miles per hour. Mac can run at a rate of 4 miles per hour. In minutes, how much faster will Mac run a 24 mile race?",
    "gold": "120",
    "answer": "First find how fast each runs. Apple = 24 miles / 3 miles per hour = <<24/3=8>>8 hours\nMac = 24 miles / 4 miles per hour = <<24/4=6>>6 hours.\nMac runs 8 hours - 6 hours = <<8-6=2>>2 hours faster.\n1 hour = 60 minutes, so, Mac runs faster by 2 hours * 60 minutes = <<2*60=120>>120 minutes.\n#### 120"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much faster Mac will run a 24-mile race compared to Apple, we need to calculate the time each takes to complete the race and then find the difference in their times.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the time it takes for Apple to run the 24-mile race. Apple's speed is 3 miles per hour. The time \\( t \\) it takes to run a distance \\( d \\) at a speed \\( s \\) is given by the formula:\n\\[ t = \\frac{d}{s} \\]\nFor Apple:\n\\[ t_{\\text{Apple}} = \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 8 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the time it takes for Mac to run the 24-mile race. Mac's speed is 4 miles per hour. Using the same formula:\n\\[ t_{\\text{Mac}} = \\frac{24 \\text{ miles}}{4 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 6 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nNow, we find the difference in time between Apple and Mac:\n\\[ \\text{Difference in time} = t_{\\text{Apple}} - t_{\\text{Mac}} = 8 \\text{ hours} - 6 \\text{ hours} = 2 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nSince the problem asks for the difference in minutes, we convert the time difference from hours to minutes. There are 60 minutes in an hour, so:\n\\[ 2 \\text{ hours} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes per hour} = 120 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nTherefore, Mac will run the race \\(\\boxed{120}\\) minutes faster than Apple.",
